     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Newborn prophylaxis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " AAP: give phytonadione to the newborn as a single IM dose of 0.5–1 mg within 1 h of birth; IM is preferred (more effective, esp vs late-onset VKDB); AAP: oral vit K not recommended; term (> 1500 g): 1 mg IM within 6 h of birth; preterm (≤ 1500 g): 0.3–0.5 mg/kg IM once."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "VKDB tx (infants):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " phytonadione 1 mg IM or SC; severe bleeding: FFP 10–15 mL/kg may be needed."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe reactions, incl fatalities, w IV and w IM phytonadione, typically resembling hypersensitivity or anaphylaxis; restrict IV and IM routes to when SC isn't feasible."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Neonates (esp premature): hemolysis, jaundice and hyperbilirubinemia may be dose-related; don't exceed the recommended dose."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
